# Line endings.
# The repo is shared between macOS and Windows. Git for Windows defaults to
# core.autocrlf=true, which would rewrite all 121 MB of committed CSVs to CRLF
# on checkout and show every data file as modified. These rules store and check
# out LF everywhere, so both machines see identical files. The one exception is
# data/raw: two of the Kaggle files ship with CRLF endings, and the raw data is
# kept byte-for-byte as downloaded, so git never converts anything in it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Data and text files: always LF.
*.csv  text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.txt  text eol=lf
*.py   text eol=lf
*.ipynb text eol=lf

# Raw source data: stored exactly as downloaded, never converted (overrides *.csv above).
data/raw/*.csv -text

# Binary: never transform, never try to merge.
*.pdf  binary
*.xlsx binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
